{"kind":"request","text":"DV-1: the `dap dev` preview and the hosted screen of one package.\n\nThe fact, from your read 9702c495 at 7a2ccc1a. `dap dev` serves the\nCounter presentation at `/index.html`, outside `/applications/`. So\n`loadApplicationScreenContext` returns null, and `main.ts` takes no\nscreen, no screen transport and no enrollment. The preview shows\n\"Import demo file\", which needs the fixed bundle of three devices.\nThe scenario actors of `dap dev` are other keys. The preview uses\nplain origin `fetch`, and the development server has no route for\nthe membership session or the head stream. The hosted screen binds\nits installed context and uses `counterEnrollment` and\n`applicationScreenTransport`.\n\nCost: a developer who runs `dap dev` on a package sees a screen that\ntakes another identity path and another transport than the screen a\nmember opens. A fault in either path shows in one place only.\n\nFirst act, no source and no run: what a developer can do in the\nCounter preview today. For each of read, act, enroll and watch, name\nthe answer and the line that gives it.\n\nThen propose one of these, with its cost:\n1. The preview serves the screen under the path and the context of\n   an installed screen, so one code path runs in both places.\n2. The preview is a named second mode, the documents state its\n   limits, and each package states which mode a witness covers.\n\nNot in DV-1: a change of the Counter package before I rule on the\nproposal.\n\nOrder: after NF-5 lands. Needs no deployment.","body":{"conditions":"Planner accepts the first act on what the Counter preview does today; planner rules on the proposal; the ruled change lands with a witness; gate passes; checker reviews the head","target_head":"4cef11d2783efaa591fac197d9a2ba093004456e","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}